"event_uuid":"c14960b1-c9e8-4e76-850f-406c40063f71","position":{"commit_sha":"baa7e149a6a4714a7058e8749893b9ba88d49a6d","position":"1786725028915291001-c14960b1-c9e8-4e76-850f-406c40063f71"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"807e3e97b8d8c4b5881672d329101d47847532922595c1cdaa232ede22654e92","event_uuid":"b3b22076-6937-4b79-bc70-07733ac4b071","position":{"commit_sha":"833a1b9a5b4c7b370b03fd52c44f1aad36f84cc5","position":"1786725033280382001-b3b22076-6937-4b79-bc70-07733ac4b071"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 1771 (commit 77d46d98439, Change-Id I7996314ac61587198e3e3b6aedf75dd69699fd23), rebased on origin/main 7c946bdf898.\n\nDetection: fsck_tracker_health.py check 4.10 — dirty_tracker_classes() classifies git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all into TRACKER_DIRTY_DELETION / TRACKER_DIRTY_LEFTOVER / TRACKER_DIRTY_TMP_EVENT (classes 1+2 counted issues; class 3 informational — a live .tmp-event-* belongs to an in-flight append). Fence: a stray *.retired preserved neither at HEAD nor on the sync remote is NOT classified (could be the only copy of an event). fsck.py JSON registration carries per-class count + paths + detail.\n\nRepair: doctor.py --repair, TWO lock windows (write_lock is non-reentrant; run_repair holds no outer lock). Backup ref refs/rebar-doctor/<utc-ts> recorded at tickets HEAD BEFORE the first mutation (no backup ref => all mutating findings unrepairable). Window 1: one scoped write_lock — deletions restored via git checkout HEAD --, leftovers MOVED into <git-common-dir>/reconverge-quarantine/<utc-ts>/ via sync._quarantine_untracked (shared implementation, no drift). Window 2 (lock released): sync.reconverge self-locks and converges the store. Class 3 marked manual, byte-identical after run.\n\nTDD: tests/unit/test_doctor_dirty_tree.py (11 tests) written first; RED proof 9/11 failed on unmodified src (ImportError dirty_tracker_classes, AttributeError doctor._quarantine_leftovers etc.; 2 vacuous negatives). Includes seeded-wedge end-to-end (all 3 classes + diverged origin), idempotence on clean store (zero changes, no backup ref), lock discipline probe (lock HELD during checkout/quarantine, NOT held entering reconverge), class-3-only store (no backup ref, no reconverge), unclassified-.retired fence.\n\nMutation pass: 9/9 manual mutants KILLED — skip backup ref, delete instead of quarantine-move, hold lock into reconverge, invert class routing, skip fsck JSON registration, _retired_source_folded forced False and forced True, drop --untracked-files=all, drop staged-deletion (D ) porcelain state, class-3 counted as issue.\n\nGates: make lint clean (complexity ratchet active=53 new=0 increased=0), make typecheck clean (538 files), LOC caps ok (doctor.py 503, fsck_tracker_health.py 384, fsck.py 325). Adjacent suites green (test_doctor.py, reconverge, union-recovery, fsck 270 passed). Full unit sweep: only pre-existing environmental failures (push/network + gh-vendor matrix + test_ref_lock remote roundtrip), all reproduced identically on unmodified src. docs/user-guide.md gained a section on the three findings and the doctor heal. Awaiting LLM-Review + Verified on change 1771.","timestamp":1786694840953577001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patchset 2 pushed on Gerrit change 1771 (same Change-Id I7996314ac61587198e3e3b6aedf75dd69699fd23), rebased onto origin/main ce54970555. Fixes the Verified -1: the raw-git-writes policy gate (scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py, merged after my original base) flagged doctor's update-ref and checkout calls — both ARE the sanctioned repair door, so they now carry inline '# raw-git-ok: <reason>' markers on the enclosing defs (backup-ref audit envelope mirroring tracker-maintenance; checkout-restore under the scoped write_lock). Gate passes locally with zero findings. Also folded in 3 of the 5 advisory LLM-Review findings: (1) classifier now uses git status --porcelain -z so C-quoted paths (spaces/quotes/non-ASCII) arrive verbatim, with rename/copy source records skipped; (2) fsck dirty lines shlex-quote paths and the JSON parser uses the declared count to locate the path-list/blurb boundary — text-to-JSON round-trip now lossless (new test with space-containing paths, RED against the old join); (3) the two untested safety contracts got tests: no-backup-ref refuses every mutation + skips reconverge + exits 1; failed checkout/quarantine mark unrepairable with reason + exit 1. Deferred with reply: rename-state (R/AD/MD) deletion classification — outside the observed wedge class, needs its own analysis. Test file now 14 tests, all green; make lint (ratchet new=0 increased=0), make typecheck (539 files), raw-git gate, and fsck/doctor suites (179+26) all clean. Awaiting fresh votes on patchset 2.","timestamp":1786721541125452001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] Gerrit change 1771 MERGED into main as 8d1dd18db2 ('Detect and repair the dirty-tracker wedge'). Vote evidence: LLM-Review +1 (PS1, 7 advisory findings — 3 folded into PS2: NUL-terminated porcelain parsing, lossless fsck path round-trip via shlex quoting + declared-count boundary, and two new safety-contract tests; 1 deferred with posted reply) and Verified +1 on PS2 after fixing the raw-git-writes gate with # raw-git-ok markers on the two sanctioned repair writes (backup ref update-ref + checkout-restore under scoped write_lock). Change reached SUBMITTABLE per Gerrit's submit rule and Submit succeeded (GET /a/changes/1771/ status=MERGED), which requires both votes green and no unresolved comments. 14/14 tests green; RED proof 9/11 on unmodified src; 9/9 mutants killed; make lint + make typecheck clean (CI re-proves).","timestamp":1786723606235526001}],"created_at":1786677403008700001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"52fc3b29-0d25-4df5-bb01-582db29e6525","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3699-c071-dd73-458b"},{"link_uuid":"8e90a36d-c9e6-4b42-8083-b63518559e59","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f05a-3cf7-69ae-4649"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nWhen the store wedges (dirty tracker tree, stale locks, stranded merge state), today's tooling is partial: `rebar fsck` checks event integrity but does not report the dirty-tree class that caused the recent P0 wedges (tracked working-tree deletions of store artifacts, untracked regenerable compaction leftovers, orphaned lock files, orphaned `.tmp-event-*`); `rebar tracker-maintenance --clean` handles only a stranded index and foreign worktree paths (verified: its `_stranded_paths`/`_foreign_worktree_paths` scans reported 0 findings while the store sat wedged with 119 tracked `.archived` deletions); the documented recovery for the live wedges was ad-hoc raw git under the write lock, recorded by hand on tickets 6ccc-0577-198c-44fa / e72e-259d-5ee7-4e73. Operators (and agents) need one sanctioned, non-destructive door: fsck DETECTS the class, doctor --repair HEALS it.\n\n## Approach\nDetection: add a tracker-dirty check to the fsck surface (src/rebar/_commands/fsck_tracker_health.py, which already owns tracker-level health lines) that classifies `git status --porcelain` output into: (1) tracked deletions of store artifacts restorable from HEAD, (2) untracked regenerable compaction leftovers (`*-SNAPSHOT.json`, `*.retired` whose retired-source is already folded), (3) orphaned `.tmp-event-*` (never auto-touched — named for manual triage), plus lock-artifact staleness reported via the existing doctor_locks scan. Each class gets a distinct finding line, and the JSON contract is wired end-to-end: fsck's JSON is produced by `_transform_json` in src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py over a fixed `_STRUCTURED_KINDS` set, so the three new tracker-dirty kinds are registered there (each emitting a `KIND: detail` line whose detail carries count + paths) — fsck.py is an explicit edit target, not an implied one.\nRepair: extend `rebar doctor --repair` (src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py's existing scan/repair_finding registry pattern) with repair actions using TWO lock windows, because the store write lock (rebar._store.lock.write_lock) is non-reentrant — doctor's own `run_repair` deliberately holds NO outer lock (its regression test pins that an outer hold starves inner per-write acquisitions), and `sync.reconverge` acquires the write lock internally. So: (window 1) the raw file-mutating steps — restore class-1 paths via `git checkout --` (non-destructive; bytes exist at HEAD) and move class-2 paths into the quarantine directory established by change 1757 (`<git-common-dir>/reconverge-quarantine/<utc-ts>/` — move, never delete) — run under one short-lived scoped write_lock acquisition, through the store seam (gitutil.run_git), and that lock is RELEASED before convergence; (window 2) the existing reconverge entry (rebar._store.sync.reconverge) is then invoked and takes the write lock itself, converging the previously wedged store in the same command. Class-3 paths are left untouched and printed. Safety envelope: before the first mutating repair, record a backup ref (`refs/rebar-doctor/<utc-ts>` pointing at the tickets HEAD) mirroring the backup-ref + durable-audit envelope `tracker-maintenance` actually provides (tracker-maintenance holds no write lock; its envelope is the backup ref plus audited raw `_git` calls — that, not a lock, is the precedent adopted here), and every action is recorded in the doctor output. Positive rationale: doctor already owns scan-classify-repair with typed findings; extending its registry avoids inventing a second repair CLI.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/fsck_tracker_health.py — tracker-dirty classification (text lines).\n- src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py — register the three tracker-dirty kinds in `_STRUCTURED_KINDS` / extend `_transform_json` so fsck --output json carries per-class counts and paths.\n- src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py — new finding types + repair actions (scoped write_lock window for file mutations; backup ref; post-release reconverge call).\n- tests/unit/test_doctor_dirty_tree.py (new) — seeded-wedge end-to-end coverage.\n- docs/user-guide.md — document the new fsck findings and doctor repairs.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: fixture tracker seeded with all three classes plus a diverged origin; `rebar fsck` names each class; `rebar doctor --repair` restores class 1, quarantines class 2 (bytes preserved), leaves class 3 in place, and the store converges (ahead/behind 0/0, `git status` clean except class 3).\n- Failure/edge: doctor --repair on a CLEAN store makes zero changes and zero commits (idempotent); the file-mutating window respects existing lock semantics (a held write lock makes it wait/fail per the lock contract rather than mutate unlocked); class-3 files are byte-identical after the run; the backup ref exists after a mutating repair and is absent after a no-op run.\n- Lock discipline: a test asserts the write lock is NOT held when reconverge is entered (mirroring doctor's existing test_run_repair_does_not_hold_a_lock_that_blocks_event_writes pattern), and IS held during the checkout/move steps.\n- JSON contract: fsck --output json carries the per-class counts and paths (via the registered kinds).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `rebar fsck` on a seeded dirty tracker reports each class with a distinct finding id in text AND in `--output json` (counts + paths); clean stores report none; checked by the new test.\n- [x] `rebar doctor --repair` heals a seeded wedge end-to-end (tree clean apart from `.tmp-event-*`, merge converged, no event bytes lost — quarantine holds moved files, backup ref recorded); checked by the end-to-end test.\n- [x] Each file-mutating repair step runs under its own scoped write-lock acquisition, the lock is released before reconverge (which self-locks), and no repair path deletes a file (moves or restores only); checked by lock-state assertions and quarantine contents in the test.\n- [x] [operator-attested] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_tracker_health.py","reason":"classify dirty-tree state into distinct finding classes"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py","reason":"repair actions under the write lock + post-repair reconverge"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py","reason":"JSON registration of the dirty-tracker finding classes (per-class count + paths + detail)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_doctor_dirty_tree.py","reason":"seeded-wedge end-to-end coverage"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"document new findings and repairs"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","fb8a-7363-e406-4e36"],["relates_to","3699-c071-dd73-458b"],["relates_to","f05a-3cf7-69ae-4649"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"fb8a-7363-e406-4e36","parent_status_uuid":"c14960b1-c9e8-4e76-850f-406c40063f71","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c925-7669-ded8-43a3","ticket_type":"story","title":"fsck detects the dirty-tree/stale-lock wedge class; doctor --repair heals it under the write lock","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f960756c-f7e7-4f7b-b0a1-05b1e2b99796","4b6c7f97-9f09-43df-b8b3-a14b1c502f5b","6f8c325d-2710-4fa0-803c-ab2c4b66c293","52fc3b29-0d25-4df5-bb01-582db29e6525","979e36a2-0909-4a9a-a49d-21593c68c092","8e90a36d-c9e6-4b42-8083-b63518559e59","9b144a8d-2c10-40f4-a12a-5afd53da6baf","2b294080-56d3-4da6-bef6-a6c3239accc1","b79654aa-8ae2-4952-8ab2-788e56626e7b","7c8fa566-9817-424f-aa79-3a01c261d47c","f53cd2c3-48c2-4702-8d3c-0f0af0acfd80","c14960b1-c9e8-4e76-850f-406c40063f71","b3b22076-6937-4b79-bc70-07733ac4b071"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786731440045841278,"uuid":"4fa6d1c2-6c12-4178-be79-a67c2a0bcb1d"}